From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.gaming.input: custom controller factories no longer crash the manager (3611)

windows.gaming.input: custom controller factories no longer crash the manager

controller_create() freed through an uninitialised IInspectable_inner when a registered
custom factory refused the provider (E_NOTIMPL): the access violation was swallowed by
the user callback handler with manager_cs still held, so every later controller event
deadlocked (dinput hotplug test: "controller added handler not invoked", hang). 2800 made
RegisterCustomFactoryForHardwareId work, which is what reaches this path.

Also completes what the custom controller protocol of the dinput hotplug test needs:
IWeakReferenceSource on the controller and the provider (weakref.c), the provider's
IHidGameControllerProvider (usage, feature/output reports), IGameControllerInputSink
OnInputResumed before OnGameControllerAdded and OnInputSuspended before
OnGameControllerRemoved, and the outer controller no longer forwards
IGameControllerProvider to the inner object. Five todo_wine marks of hotplug.c that
now pass are removed.
---
